  message: "Done in PR #1330 (merged, dev 6a3b004ec1). The third-party crypto rows were moved to community files by WI-nopam (#1317); this implements the ADD-ONLY rule: a sanitizer loaded from a file declaring provenance: community (TaintSanitizer.community, stamped at load) is not a barrier in either walk; the flow is reported, its evidence row names it (withheld_sanitizers), and the violated verdict carries a withheld_community_sanitizer caveat saying how to vouch (copy the file into taint_sanitizers.d, delete the line). Community SOURCES still mint taint (they add). BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE on merged dev: rotate() Fernet decrypt -> seal_and_store encrypt -> write, claim plaintext never reaches host_fs: violated rc 1, sanitized_flows 0, caveat withheld_community_sanitizer, withheld_sanitizers [cryptography.fernet.Fernet.encrypt, ...] (was inconclusive rc 2 with sanitized_flows 1 on dev a196aaddb5); vouched control (test_community_sanitizer_is_not_credited.py): the file copied into taint_sanitizers.d without the line -> sanitized_flows 1 + user_supplied_sanitizer. PRE-REGISTERED A/B (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dikit_09302026/RESULT.md): 6 repos using cryptography (podman-compose feast nova mlflow litellm airflow), 54 verdicts: IDENTICAL, 0 refutations, ZERO MEASURED EFFECT -- no arm-A flow was sanitized by any moved row. arti (the only Rust repo, aes-gcm/ring/hkdf rows) NOT measured: it hangs in two more repository walks (INV-pivir reopened); ceph dropped for cost. The ADR-0061 Consequences prediction (more violated plaintext verdicts) is not borne out on this cohort, which has no flow it applies to."  # 2fd9
